1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,133
In this video you will learn how to start Kefir Hub, find your way around its

2
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:08,067
screen, switch tabs and change the language.

3
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:11,400
Kefir Hub is a homebrew app that comes with Kefir.

4
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:15,533
It starts from the Homebrew Menu, like any other homebrew app.

5
00:00:15,533 --> 00:00:19,067
The quickest way into the Homebrew Menu is the Album.

6
00:00:19,067 --> 00:00:21,067
Select Kefir Hub and press A.

7
00:00:21,067 --> 00:00:23,067
But how you start it matters.

8
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:26,067
From the Album, Kefir Hub gets little memory.

9
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:31,400
Large compressed NSZ games will most likely not install, and the web server runs

10
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,400
slower.

11
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:38,733
To give Kefir Hub all the memory, hold R while you start any installed game, and

12
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:41,600
keep holding until the Homebrew Menu opens.

13
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:44,267
Use this way whenever you install games.

14
00:00:44,267 --> 00:00:46,533
An icon of its own is even easier.

15
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:51,200
On the Tools tab press plus and choose "Install Title Mode forwarder".

16
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:53,200
Confirm the install.

17
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:56,000
When it is done, go back to the HOME Menu.

18
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,800
The new icon always starts Kefir Hub with all the memory.

19
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:05,400
On the first launch Kefir Hub shows a page in the console's language: start Hub from

20
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,400
its HOME Menu icon.

21
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,400
Press A and choose a language.

22
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:12,467
Another language: Hub warns and restarts once.

23
00:01:12,467 --> 00:01:17,733
If some profiles on the console are not linked to a Nintendo Account, Kefir Hub

24
00:01:17,733 --> 00:01:19,733
offers to link them.

25
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:22,267
There is a separate video about users.

26
00:01:22,267 --> 00:01:24,267
This is the main screen.

27
00:01:24,267 --> 00:01:26,267
At the top is the header.

28
00:01:26,267 --> 00:01:31,733
On its left: the Kefir Hub version, the screen name and your position in the list.

29
00:01:31,733 --> 00:01:37,133
On the right: the Kefir, firmware and Atmosphère versions, the Wi-Fi name and the

30
00:01:37,133 --> 00:01:39,133
console's IP address.

31
00:01:39,133 --> 00:01:44,200
Then two bars with free space in the console memory and on the microSD card.

32
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,267
Then the clock and the battery.

33
00:01:46,267 --> 00:01:50,400
The MTP and FTP badges show whether these servers are running.

34
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:52,733
A green dot means the server is on.

35
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:57,800
The bottom line shows the buttons that work on this screen and what they do.

36
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:00,867
If you are not sure what to press, look there.

37
00:02:00,867 --> 00:02:02,867
A opens, starts or confirms.

38
00:02:02,867 --> 00:02:04,867
B goes back.

39
00:02:04,867 --> 00:02:10,267
X selects an item so you can act on several at once, and Y inverts the selection.

40
00:02:10,267 --> 00:02:13,733
ZL and ZR jump to the first and last item of a list.

41
00:02:13,733 --> 00:02:16,400
In long lists, L and R page up and down.

42
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,400
The main screen has two tabs.

43
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:21,467
Homebrew lists the homebrew apps on your card.

44
00:02:21,467 --> 00:02:23,467
Press R to go to Tools.

45
00:02:23,467 --> 00:02:28,867
The Tools tab has everything else: File Browser, Game Tools with games, saves and

46
00:02:28,867 --> 00:02:33,200
cheats, Themes, Updater, and Software with the App Store and DBI.

47
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:37,467
The Tools tile holds Module Manager, Fan curve, Wi-Fi and Users.

48
00:02:37,467 --> 00:02:42,200
Kefir Settings are console settings; Settings are for Kefir Hub itself.

49
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:45,667
Console Transfer exchanges data with another device.

50
00:02:45,667 --> 00:02:47,933
Screens open on top of each other.

51
00:02:47,933 --> 00:02:49,933
B closes the current one.

52
00:02:49,933 --> 00:02:54,000
Minus closes them all and takes you back to the Homebrew tab.

53
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,867
From the Tools tab, L or B also take you back to Homebrew.

54
00:02:57,867 --> 00:03:02,133
Plus opens the options panel of the current screen on the right.

55
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:07,200
Move the cursor onto an entry and a short description appears at the bottom.

56
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:09,800
A runs the action or flips the setting.

57
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,800
B or plus closes the panel.

58
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:16,467
A grey entry is not available right now, and its description says why.

59
00:03:16,467 --> 00:03:20,733
In dialogs, move between the buttons with the D-pad and press A.

60
00:03:20,733 --> 00:03:24,267
B picks the first button, usually Back, No or Cancel.

61
00:03:24,267 --> 00:03:28,067
Plus picks the last one, the button that does the action.

62
00:03:28,067 --> 00:03:31,733
Some risky actions ask you to hold A until a bar fills.

63
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:37,067
When text is needed, some fields offer "Manual (Keyboard)" or "From Phone / PC".

64
00:03:37,067 --> 00:03:42,600
The second shows a QR code and an address, so you can type long text on your phone.

65
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:47,800
The touch screen works too: tap an item to select it and tap again to open it.

66
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,800
Now let's change the language.

67
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:53,600
Open Tools, Settings, the General category, and Language.

68
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,600
Pick a language.

69
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:58,000
Kefir Hub asks "Restart Kefir Hub?".

70
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,600
Choose Restart so the new language applies everywhere.

71
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:05,200
Copies, installs and downloads show a progress window.

72
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:09,533
Some tasks can run in the background, for example the web server.

73
00:04:09,533 --> 00:04:14,000
Press R3 and the window shrinks to a badge in the top right corner.

74
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,800
Press R3 again or tap the badge to bring the window back.

75
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:20,667
B stops the task, but Kefir Hub asks first.

76
00:04:20,667 --> 00:04:23,067
Do not press HOME during a transfer.

77
00:04:23,067 --> 00:04:28,667
While you are in the HOME Menu the console pauses Kefir Hub, and the transfer stops.

78
00:04:28,667 --> 00:04:33,800
If you want the Album to open Kefir Hub directly, turn on Settings, Homebrew,

79
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:35,800
"Replace hbmenu on exit".

80
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:41,000
When you turn it off again, Kefir Hub offers to restore the old Homebrew Menu.

81
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
That covers the basics.

82
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:48,067
For more, read the Kefir Hub and Getting started pages in the documentation.
